<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart -- April 25-27.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart -- April 25-27.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final</p>
<p>data for the top 10 movies at the April 25-27 box office,</p>
<p>according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		    Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Volcano		     $14,581,740	 $  ----</p>
<p>2. Romy and Michele's</p>
<p>    High School Reunion    $ 7,429,406	 $  ----</p>
<p>3. Anaconda		    $ 7,318,954	 $ 43,231,457</p>
<p>4. Liar Liar		   $ 7,186,130	 $143,839,650</p>
<p>5. The Saint		   $ 5,007,093	 $ 48,610,631</p>
<p>6. Murder at 1600	    $ 4,825,209	 $ 15,284,092</p>
<p>7. Grosse Pointe Blank     $ 3,098,353	 $ 18,152,209</p>
<p>8. Scream			$ 1,405,839	 $ 93,021,393</p>
<p>9. The Devil's Own	   $ 1,154,808	 $ 41,019,604</p>
<p>10 Chasing Amy		 $ 1,111,989	 $  3,886,506</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Volcano&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Romy and Michele's High School Reunion&quot; and &quot;Grosse Pointe Blank&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co. &quot;Chasing Amy&quot; and &quot;Scream&quot; are released by Disney's Miramax Films.</p>
<p>&quot;Anaconda&quot; and &quot;The Devil's Own&quot; are released by Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Liar Liar&quot; and &quot;That Old Feeling&quot; are released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;The Saint&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;Murder at 1600&quot; is released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
